    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484-a1">

                <pb facs="0694" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg606"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 579.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Said Pasha to Mr. Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to your note to me of the 10th instant, No. 126, I hasten to inform you
                    that the five individuals arrested in connection with the burning of Mr.
                    Bartlett’s house at Bourdour have been sent for trial before a competent
                    tribunal at Smyrna, the result of which will be transmitted to you.</p>
                <p>As to the authorities who may have been negligent in this affair, an inquiry is
                    now being carried oh with the view of establishing their responsibility.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
